# SSIMULACRA2 for every encoding in the live squintly corpus.
#
# corpus:        imazen26-v5-test-noai (168 sources / 4032 encodings, test split, no AI strata)
# produced by:   cargo run --release --bin squintly-score
# commit:        see `git log -1` at 2026-08-06
# implementation: fast-ssim2 0.8.2 (imazen), CPU, imgref feature
# runtime:       1570s wall, 6-way concurrency, peak RSS 1.10 GiB (run-heavy)
# coverage:      4032/4032 encodings — no failures, no gaps
# range:         -53.5 .. 94.5, median 69.3
#
# The encodings are FETCHED FROM THE LIVE STORE and decoded, not re-encoded, so
# these scores are of exactly the bytes observers were shown.
#
# Nothing existing could be reused: all 16 parquets under
# /mnt/v/output/imazen-26-features/ are zensim SOURCE features with no metric
# columns, and the one sweep carrying `score_ssim2`
# (/mnt/v/output/dense-bal1000-sweep-2026-06-25.omni.tsv, 444k rows) is 100%
# zenjxl on differently-named files — a codec this corpus does not contain.
#
# Calibration derived from this file, against 84 live human comparisons:
#   ssim2 gap 0-5   n=16  94% human agreement
#   ssim2 gap 5-10  n=44 100%
#   ssim2 gap 10+   n=24 100%
# Median adjacent-rung gaps on the [15,30,45,60,80,92] ladder:
#   15->30 17.3 | 30->45 7.9 | 45->60 5.7 | 60->80 8.0 | 80->92 6.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-06 by the 17-rung ladder (corpus v6, 11,424 encodings).
# Results of the rebuild, same scorer, --fs against the local store:
#
#   max adjacent-rung ssim2 gap   17.3  ->  5.8   (1 of 16 gaps still over 5)
#   encodings scoring >= 90       ~0    ->  863 / 11,424
#   range                         -53.5..94.5  ->  -53.5..96.6
#   median at q100 by codec       jpegli 93.4 | libjpeg-turbo 89.2
#                                 libavif 88.9 | libwebp 87.6
#   runtime                       3491s, peak RSS 1.11 GiB, 168/168 sources
#
